<title>GERMANY: Viag -no plans to sell Computer 2000 unit.</title>
<headline>Viag -no plans to sell Computer 2000 unit.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified utility Viag AG said on Friday that it had no plans to sell off its Computer 2000 subsidiary, but said it planned to restructure Computer 2000's U.S. business.</p>
<p>Computer 2000 was going through a weak phase because of its U.S. business and some kind of reorganisation in the United States was necessary, Obermeier said in an interview with Reuters.</p>
<p>Earlier Obermeier said that Computer 2000 had reached break-even in 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
